# Frontend

## Stack

Next.js 16 App Router · React 19 · Tailwind 4 (CSS-first config, no
`tailwind.config.js`) · shadcn/ui · TanStack Query · react-hook-form + zod.

Server components by default. `'use client'` only where interaction requires it,
and as low in the tree as possible.

**No chart library.** The wheel is a hand-rolled SVG radar. Eight to ten points
with three overlaid polygons needs exact control, and a charting dependency
costs more than it gives.

**No global state library.** TanStack Query for server state, React state for
the rest.

## Visual voice

Calm like a paper planner, not an admin console. Warm off-white canvas
(`#fefdfc`), warm ink (`#25221e`) at varying opacity, Inter, and our navy as
the only accent. Hierarchy comes from type and space. No drop shadows, no
uppercase table headers, no boxed data tables. Lists are hairline rows. The
active nav is a warm peach wash with ink text, not a blue fill.

## The radar component

The signature element of the app. Requirements:

- Accepts N axes, not a hardcoded eight — the business wheel varies per member.
- Up to three polygons: today (filled, solid), one year (solid line), five years
  (dashed). The comparison view instead overlays two dated cycles.
- Renders from a `viewBox` and scales to its container. Never fixed pixel sizes.
- A missing score is a gap, not a zero. Do not plot null as the centre.
- Labels stay legible at 320px — shorten in the data, never clip in the render.
- Accessible: a table of the same values is present for screen readers, visually
  hidden if the design calls for it.

`/radar` is the standalone preview against hardcoded wireframe scores.

## Mobile

Mobile-first, and mobile is a real use case: members update tasks on a phone
between meetings. Test every screen at 375px.

- Bottom tab bar on mobile — Tasks, Life, Business, Board. Sidebar on desktop.
- Touch targets 44px minimum.
- Score entry is a stepper or a select, never a free-text number field. It is a
  0–10 value and the keyboard is the wrong tool.
- Tables become stacked rows below `md`. Never a horizontal scroll on a data
  table the user needs to read.
- The wheel goes full width above the score grid on mobile.

## Screen-share legibility

The task list is shared on a video call. Generous row height, no truncated task
titles, no horizontal scroll at laptop width, and enough contrast to survive
video compression.

## PWA

- `@serwist/next`, service worker at `src/sw.ts`, disabled in development.
- **Precache the app shell and static assets only.** Never cache authenticated
  Supabase responses or any route under `(app)`. A stale wheel is worse than a
  spinner, and a cached response served to the wrong session is a privacy
  breach — which is the one thing this product cannot afford.
- Offline fallback states plainly what is unavailable and what still works.
- `manifest.json`: name, short_name, 192 and 512 icons including maskable,
  `display: standalone`.

## Copy

Sentence case. Plain verbs. No exclamation marks. A button names what happens
and keeps the same word through the flow — "Save rating" produces "Rating
saved". Empty states invite an action. Errors say what happened and what to do.
Never apologise.

## Accessibility

Visible keyboard focus. Respect `prefers-reduced-motion`. Colour never the only
carrier of meaning — the three wheel polygons differ by line style as well as
hue. Target Lighthouse accessibility ≥ 95.
